Hi Stuart,

an easy way would be to use the day summary in order to calculate the weighted averages manually.

Other than that, I suppose you could replace the respective lines with the following in the g.report.part5 function using edit(g.report.part5()).
However, this is a guess and I don't know much about R or the rest of the script so I am not sure if there could be any side effects.

Good luck,
David

# Calculate, weighted and plain mean of all variables
# add column to define what are weekenddays and weekdays as needed for function agg_plainNweighted
OF3$daytype = 0
OF3$daytype[which(OF3$weekday == "Saturday" | OF3$weekday == "Friday")] = "WE"
OF3$daytype[which(OF3$weekday == "Sunday" | OF3$weekday == "Monday" |
OF3$weekday == "Tuesday" | OF3$weekday == "Wednesday" |
OF3$weekday == "Thursday")] = "WD"
OF3 = as.data.frame(OF3)

